WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:01.543
- [Narrator] From a distance,

00:00:01.543 --> 00:00:03.960
this may not look like a village.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.090
But get up close and you'll
see it's a small settlement

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:11.314
built into the heart into
debris of an erupted volcano.

00:00:11.314 --> 00:00:14.397
(quiet upbeat music)

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.260
Located in the northwest corner of Iran

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.880
is the ancient village of Kandovan.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.350
These unusual looking peaks were created

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.400
when now dormant volcano
Mount Sahand erupted

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.290
thousands of years ago.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.610
Over time, the volcanic
ash, lava, and debris

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.940
hardened to stone and the unique shapes

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.393
are the result of weathering.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:40.180
Inside the peaks are livable
caves that have been turned

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.890
into homes by the local villagers.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.850
Surprisingly, they are some of
the most economical on earth.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.200
The cave's insulation means no heating

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.773
or cooling is required.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.913
There's also a mosque, a
public bath, and a school.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.250
The term Kandovan is derived
from the Persian word

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.970
kando meaning beehives.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:07.520
And fittingly, 600 people call these hives

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.020
their humble home.

